BND-20: print 0 instead of NaN in the Flow Classification table when no routing step falls in the reporting period

DefaultReportPlugin divides the flow-class, normal-flow-limited and
inlet-control times by routing_stats.report_time, which is 0 when no routing
step falls after REPORT_START ([EVENTS] outside the reporting window, or a
client that ends the run before the first step). The node and storage
averages are already guarded with max(report_steps, 1); use 1 s here as
well, so the zero times print as 0.00. Results with at least one step are
unchanged.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply BND-20_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/plugins/DefaultReportPlugin.cpp b/src/engine/plugins/DefaultReportPlugin.cpp
index 36a8dbb..6fdb3d4 100644
--- a/src/engine/plugins/DefaultReportPlugin.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/plugins/DefaultReportPlugin.cpp
@@ -2953,7 +2953,9 @@ void DefaultReportPlugin::write_results(std::FILE* f,
 "\n  Conduit               Length    Dry  Dry   Dry   Crit  Crit  Crit  Crit  Ltd   Ctrl  "
 "\n  -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------");
 
-        const double total_secs = ctx.routing_stats.report_time;
+        // No routing step in the reporting period: every time below is 0.
+        const double total_secs = (ctx.routing_stats.report_time > 0.0)
+            ? ctx.routing_stats.report_time : 1.0;
 
         for (int j = 0; j < ctx.n_links(); ++j) {
             auto uj = static_cast<std::size_t>(j);
